  "scenario": "A production compute cluster's job throughput has dropped about 30% over the past two weeks and has not recovered. The decline followed a data-hall maintenance window in which cooling was serviced and a line card was reseated. A rack inlet-temperature sensor has been reading warmer than its historical band, and the operations team's leading theory is that the room is running hot, so they are considering increasing cooling. Standard host metrics look broadly normal. The cooling plant, power distribution, storage QoS, and environmental controls are all adjustable, and portable environmental equipment is available. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available controls, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the loss and what to do about it.",
